# Copy to .env. Only non-secrets belong here.
#
# Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time and is trivially extractable from the APK. The NS and TomTom keys live in
# apps/api/.env and are never read from this file.

# Where the API is, from the phone's point of view.
#
# Leave it unset while developing: the app falls back to the machine serving
# Metro, on port 3000, which is the same machine running `npm run dev:api`.
# Set it when that guess is wrong, and it will be in three cases:
#
#   1. The API moved to another port because 3000 was taken. It says so on
#      startup: "API listening on http://localhost:3000".
#   2. You are on a preview build, which has no Metro to infer a host from.
#   3. The API is not on your machine at all.
#
# Use the machine's LAN address, never localhost or 127.0.0.1: on a phone those
# mean the phone. `ipconfig` on Windows, under the wifi adapter.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.149:3000

# Extra logging in the app. Off by default.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEBUG=true
